<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bera, Count of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/844">844</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bera was the first count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> captured the city in 801, a Goth probably descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-gellone">William of Gellone</a>. Accused of treason and of dealings with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, he lost a judicial duel at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> in 820 and was deposed and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>, where he died. His fall left the Spanish March to Frankish counts and, later, to the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bera-count-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="Bera, Count of Barcelona" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bera.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Bera's origins are mostly unknown, though it seems certain that he was a Visigoth. In 790 he was given the governorship of the counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razes">Razès</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conflent">Conflent</a>, possibly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-gellone">William of Gellone</a>, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> and cousin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>. In 796 Sa'dun al Ruayni, the Wali of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, tried to break his allegiance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hakam-i">Al-Hakam I</a>, emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, and in April 797 he travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> to offer the city to Charlemagne in return for help.</p><p>An assembly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> in the spring of 800 agreed to send <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, but Sa'dun changed his mind and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> laid siege to the city. Starving, its Visigoth population surrendered on 3 April 801 and handed over the new wali, Harun; Louis entered the next day. Bera, who had served in the besieging army, was soon invested as count.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>Bera took part in the Frankish campaigns of 804, 808 and 809 to push the border of the Marca Hispanica to the River Ebro. In 804 he, Adhemar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narbonne">Narbonne</a> and Borrell of Ausona covered the western flank of Louis's army, while Louis besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> without success. In 808, according to the biographer known as the Astronomer, the garrison of Tortosa was alerted when horse dung from Bera's river crossing floated past the town, and he was forced to retreat. In 809 Tortosa was besieged for forty days.</p><p>Bera was probably the strongest promoter of peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, urged on by his mother and by the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, and the Frankish court signed a three-year treaty in 812. In 811 he had witnessed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s will. When war resumed in 815, a mercenary Visigothic army beat back an attack on Barcelona led by Ubayd Allah Abu Marwan, and a new three-year truce was concluded in February 817.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Gaucelm, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a>, and his brother Bernard argued that Bera's truces hindered attempts to force the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basques">Basques</a> and Aragón to recognise the empire's authority. At a general assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> in February 820, Gaucelm's Visigoth lieutenant Sanila accused Bera of infidelity and perfidy, and the case was settled, as was customary, by a duel in the palace. Bera lost and was deprived of his counties, but Emperor Louis I, who did not believe him a traitor, commuted the death penalty to exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>. He was succeeded as count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> by Rampon.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Bera, Count of Barcelona” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Its first count, the Goth <b>Bera</b>, was deposed in 820.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-barcelona">County of Barcelona</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.98,2.82&amp;year=834" aria-label="Girona on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4618 669 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Bera, Count of Barcelona"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5068 939h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5068 939h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.98,2.82&amp;year=834">What was here in 834 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
